From: BearddOddity <beardedoddity@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:36:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] Beardd's Wayfarer 1.2.0: a small keys panel at the
 side; the mod's words in the game's language

Keys panel (the player: "way too big and in the way, too many times is Beardd's Wayfarer labeled, it shouldn't be center of
the screen in case an enemy appears"): docked small at the left edge, the middle of the view clear; the name every module
shares said once, the actions grouped by module (groupKeys).

Words (the player: "sync with DFO language so we don't need to create translation"): the handle gains dfo.t(key, en, args),
read through the game's own text core in the language the player chose, the module's English where the table has no row.
Every word the three modules show goes through it under module.<id>.* keys; no translations are shipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
