 The game binds F5 (character sheet), F6 (inventory), F8 (screenshot), F9/F11 (quick save/load), F10 (HUD) and the letters, digits and arrows in play; in dialogs and the maps it binds F1-F8 again. The modules use F2, F3, F4, F7 (and Shift with F2, F3, F4, F7) - none a gameplay default - and each key does nothing unless the HUD has drawn in the last 400 ms, so a dialog, a menu or a map that uses the same F key is never also answered by a module. `test/mods1_api.test.js` reads the game's default bindings and fails if a module takes one, if two modules share a key, or if a key is not gated.
 
-**The keys are the player's.** Shift+F1 (no gameplay default of the game's) opens the keys panel (`src/mods/keysPanel.js`; also the Modules card's "Change module keys" button): every module action with the key it has now. Choose one (click, or Tab and Enter) and press the new key; Escape cancels, Backspace puts the module's own key back. A key another module action has is refused by name; Shift+F1 and the menus' keys (Escape, Tab, Enter, Backspace) are never given; a plain letter, digit, arrow or Space is allowed with a warning that the game may use it too. The choice is the bus's (`setKey`, kept under `dfjs-module-keys` in the game's own storage) and takes effect at once: the host hands every key press to `pressKey`, which answers it by the keys as they stand. While the panel is open it takes every press and frees the pointer. Its words come through the game's text core (`modBus.js` `moduleKeyWords`); the loader's host, with no text core, hands the same panel English.
+**The keys are the player's.** Shift+F1 (no gameplay default of the game's) opens the keys panel (`src/mods/keysPanel.js`; also the Modules card's "Change module keys" button) - small, docked at the left edge so the middle of the view stays clear, the name its modules share said once and their actions grouped by module: every module action with the key it has now. Choose one (click, or Tab and Enter) and press the new key; Escape cancels, Backspace puts the module's own key back. A key another module action has is refused by name; Shift+F1 and the menus' keys (Escape, Tab, Enter, Backspace) are never given; a plain letter, digit, arrow or Space is allowed with a warning that the game may use it too. The choice is the bus's (`setKey`, kept under `dfjs-module-keys` in the game's own storage) and takes effect at once: the host hands every key press to `pressKey`, which answers it by the keys as they stand. While the panel is open it takes every press and frees the pointer. Its words come through the game's text core (`modBus.js` `moduleKeyWords`); the loader's host, with no text core, hands the same panel English.
 
