 PROBE (no suite row - it needs `npx wrangler`): `npm run account` (tools/accountProbe.mjs) stands `server-account/` up in a REAL workerd, applies the real migrations to a real D1 through wrangler's ledger, and drives the whole account lifecycle AND (AUDIT-312 F4) a whole cloud-save round trip against workerd's own R2 - 36 checks. IT EXISTS BECAUSE THE SUITE WAS GREEN OVER A WORKER THAT COULD NOT BOOT: a module Worker reads every named export of its entrypoint as an entrypoint, `server-account/src/index.js` exported four constants, and workerd refused to start - while `test/accountworker.test.js` passed BECAUSE it imported those very names. Importability is not deployability. It also measures what the suite can only assume: Ed25519 exists in that runtime (it is not in every WebCrypto and the token design rests on it), PBKDF2 at 210,000 costs 36ms there, and a token the Worker SIGNS verifies against the key the Worker PUBLISHES, with a stranger's key and a bent byte as the negative controls. AUDIT-312 F4 ADDED ACC2's HALF, and the reason is the same one: ACC2 declared a new BINDING (`SAVES`, an R2 bucket) and seven routes, and nothing in this tree asked whether that binding is really bound - a binding that is ABSENT does not crash, it answers `no-storage`, which reaches a player as "Cloud saves are unavailable right now" with a green suite and a green deploy behind it. It drives the guest wall, a blob refused without a card, the card, the bytes back BYTE FOR BYTE as an octet-stream, the shot bounded apart from the save, another account refused a read and a delete, and the player's own delete taking the object as well as the row. AND IT WAS ONLY EVER CORRECT ONCE: `wrangler --local` REUSES its state, so run two registered a username run one had taken and logged in with a password run one's recovery check had changed - six failures about the last run rather than about the service, and a migration check reading "no migrations to apply" as "no migrations". It stands on a